DESCRIPTION:The Toronto Photography Group\n## Tickets at www.wtpg.ngo\n\n#
 # Time & Location\n\nDec 13\, 2026\, 11:30 AM – 1:00 PM\nRevprint Studio
  205\, 146 Thirtieth St\, Etobicoke\, ON M8W 3C4\, Canada\n\n## About the 
 event\n\nAbout the event\n\n11:30 am 1pm session\nStudio- Revprint Studio 
 205\nInstructor -Phil Sutherland\n\nModel Dane Halo -[https://www.instagra
 m.com/theredbomb_model/](https://www.instagram.com/theredbomb_model/)\n\nJ
 oin us for this fun and educational small group lighting workshop with Mod
 el \,Dane Halo\, T\n**Workshop Details:** This is an amazing opportunity t
 o light and shoot an talented international model in studio with some beau
 tiful light set ups with Elinchrom modifiers . We will be creating 3x ligh
 ting set ups and creating some lingerie and sheer images using modifiers t
 o soften and ahape the light .\nDo you aspire to learn the secrets of beau
 tiful and creative soft and crisp lighting techniques?\nWe are dedicated t
 o lighting and sharing our photographic knowledge with you. Our small\, in
 timate workshop with professional instructors is designed to cater to your
  interests. Throughout the workshop\, we will discuss the specific lightin
 g setups for each scenario\, explaining the choice of modifiers and angles
  to effectively illuminate the subject and accessories.\n\n\\*\\*Instructo
 r:\\*\\*Phil Sutherland **:** The exceptionally awesome model Dane Halo. H
 er remarkable posing skills will contribute to creating stunning images du
 ring the workshop.\nTo ensure a high-quality experience for participants\,
  we are limiting the workshop to a maximum of only 5 participants.\n\nAs a
 n indigenous-led\, not-for-profit arts group\, we are dedicated to serving
  the artistic community and advocating for the photographic arts. At our c
 ore\, we believe in sharing knowledge and the joy of photography with the 
 community. We strive to make art accessible to everyone and work hard to b
 ring arts programming to the community.\n\n**Workshop Details:**\n\n* Maxi
 mum Participants: 5\n* Workshop Fee: CAD$145 plus hst and vendor fee\n\n**
 Items to Bring:**\n\n* Camera/Lenses of choice (DSLR\, medium format\, or 
 mirrorless)\n* Fully charged battery\n* Freshly formatted memory card(s)\n
 * General lenses\n* Pen and paper (if you wish to take notes)\n\nSo that y
 ou know\, tripods or camera supports are not required for this workshop.\n
 **Triggers:** We provide wireless triggers for most mainstream camera type
 s. Please feel free to email us to confirm compatibility with your camera.
 \n**Model Release:** A West Toronto Photography Group model release form\,
  will be provided to each participant for non-commercial use and training 
